# P1a-CTL2 (CONTROL, the window image with every Lever N flag off): the prefix exactness-shared arm on the PRODUCTION audited profile (c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit) served by the window image
# tp4-serve-11. It stands in for W-0's P1a-CTL, which timed out on the whole-pool audit (partial result 8/8 byte-exact hits at 4.6k-6.4k tokens, scratchpad/tp4/p1a-partial) and never gave a verdict.
# DEVIATION, stated: this is the window image's engine with its Lever N and prefix flags exactly as the production profile sets them, not tp4-serve-10 itself. The production base image has no region read
# (tp4-serve-10 + the graft as a mount is not a mechanism the workflow has), and S0-CTL's hashes (production reference v579) tie the window image to production's bytes with the flags off.
# NEEDS KVQ: the arm audits every request (48) and only the region read makes that fit (docs/prefix-audit-cost.md); the prefix gate also refuses it before any container boots on an image without the graft.
# VERDICT: PASS = the arm verdict PASS and every ship P1 read (eight agents, every pair identical, a packed round with 2+ live users, hits byte-equal to their solo cold twins, window digests equal, no program
# compiled by a hit after its cold twin); FAIL = any FAIL (a PRODUCTION FINDING: the same prefix route serves production, the owner decides prefix-reuse.off); otherwise NO-VERDICT (TIMEBOX, INFRA, NOT_EXERCISED).
# Box 120 = 1.5 times an 80-minute high end (docs/prefix-audit-cost.md, 'A P1-CTL re-run'); the prefix gate clips every arm's docker timeout to what the box has left, so a slow audit ends the job as a TIMEBOX.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the chained session pack (tp4-session-0808-jobs). Names no rig, card, host or registry.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-11
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=exactness-shared
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=120
